{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v1","paper":"erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:actual-orbit","the tail recurrence and a quadratic\nbound","<p><em> The series defining <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> converge. For every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>8640</mn><mn>343</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>90</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, either <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> is integral at some index (and hence\nat every later index), or <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>31</mn></math></span> at arbitrarily large indices.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:admissible-modular-minors","the same minors modulo integers\ncoprime to <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>30</mn></math></span>","<p><em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, there are injective maps <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>:</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, chosen\nindependently of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span>, such that for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> coprime to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>30</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, the selected <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> kernel matrix has unit\ndeterminant over <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, with each reciprocal prime power interpreted by its modular\ninverse.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:cell","cells and jumps","<p><em> The running\nLCM is constant when the three integer logarithms are constant. A jump\nin exactly one logarithm multiplies it by the corresponding prime. The\nfirst <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span> positive powers of each\nprime, together with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></span>, form <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> distinct points.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:consumer","least positive residues","<p><em> If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> is a positive integer with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≡</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>F</mi><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>W</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>lpr</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:denominator-reduction","rationality gives positive integer\ntails","<p><em> If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></math></span> in lowest\nterms, where <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi></msup><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>w</mi></msup><mi>B</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, then for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>90</mn><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:distinct-height-235","the sum over distinct running LCMs for\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>","<p><em> The number <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>𝒟</mi></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></math></span> is\nirrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:dyadic-alphabet","integer coefficients and four possible\nbases","<p><em> For every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> is a positive integer and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. The word “numerator”\ndoes not impose the positional-digit restriction <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span>; that restriction need not\nhold.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:exact-onset","the first index at which the\ndenominator clears","<p><em> Under the same lowest-terms hypothesis, put\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi></msup><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></math></span> and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>den</mi></math></span> denote the positive\nreduced denominator. For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>den</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nConsequently <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> is integral\nexactly when <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. The first\nsuch <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span> can be found by integer\ncomparisons, without logarithmic rounding.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:fibre-prop","grouping terms with the same running\nLCM","<p><em> For a finite exponent box <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℬ</mi></mrow></math></span>, set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>13</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>H</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:finite-cut-rank","rank of a matrix of threshold\ncolumns","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> lie in a field with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></math></span> write <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math></span> for the length-<span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> column with a <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></span> in each of the first <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span> coordinates and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> thereafter. A matrix whose distinct\ncolumns are <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span> in a nonempty set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> has rank <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:infinite-rank","no finite separation of the kernel","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> be primes with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span>, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span>. For every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> there are injective maps\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>:</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> such\nthat, for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo movablelimits=\"true\">det</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Consequently, for no finite <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> do there exist rational-valued\nfunctions <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>, satisfying </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>for all </mtext></mstyle><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:lcm","the running least common multiple","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> be pairwise distinct\nprimes and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. Then the running\nleast common multiple is given by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:two-prime-transcendence","both two-prime sums","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span> be distinct primes. Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo></mrow></msup></math></span>. Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> sum the reciprocal running LCM at every positive <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>-smooth integer, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>𝒟</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> count each distinct\nrunning LCM once. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>10</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>𝒟</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mrow><mi>ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Both numbers are transcendental.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-269-three-prime-running-lcm#res:windowconsumer","a residue criterion for irrationality","<p><em> The number <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is irrational if\nand only if </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>8</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>for every </mtext><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> with </mtext><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> and every </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>there are </mtext><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> such that</mtext><msub><mi>lpr</mi><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>"]]}
